---
// The 404, designed (journey-site#77) -- the book's answer to Other Memory's "Nothing was written
// down here." Starlight injects its own 404 route; Astro gives a project page at the same path
// precedence, and this one wears Starlight's layout through <StarlightPage> so the spine, the
// header and the theme stay. Site template, not content: nothing here is the chronicler's.
// The byline is deliberately absent -- there is no chapter for her to sign -- and check-emitted.py
// does not count 404.html among the pages that must carry it.
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
---
<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: 'This chapter was never written.', tableOfContents: false, prev: false, next: false }}>
  <div class="book-notfound">
    <p class="book-notfound-code"><b>404</b> &mdash; not in the chronicle</p>
    <p>
      The chronicle is told in order, and this address is not in it &mdash; a chapter that was never
      written, or one that was and is deliberately left out. The spine on the left has every chapter
      there is.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/awakening/">Back to the title page</a></li>
      <li><a href="/colophon/">Who keeps these records, and why</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</StarlightPage>
